id: pm-pllp78
title: "GH-1591: guarded terminal updates conflict with their own scalar write and misreport compensation"
description: "Sequential timestamp-guarded SDK update persists scalar edits, then refuses its own terminal transition as upsert_match_changed while the journal reports compensated. Independently reproduced in an isolated current-build fixture on Node26.12.1."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: "gh:1591",sdk,transactions
created_at: "2026-10-25T17:24:01.820Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-25T22:45:46.676Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-25T22:24:41.855Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-25T22:24:41.855Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Matching initial timestamp guard plus scalar edits and terminal transition succeeds without self-conflict; stale starting guards refuse before any item/history writes; internal steps retain lock-held writer safety; partial mutation is truthfully reported or compensated; sequential lifecycle/history/journal regressions cover both success and refusal.
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: Advance only the active guard after its own durable writes; attribute every scalar and terminal mutation; reconcile opt-in pending partial steps with prefix-bound exact history versions and preserve competing writes or ambiguous recovery journals.
expected_result: "Guarded multi-write updates close successfully without self-conflict, and failed batches restore only provably owned effects, including same-clock writes and interrupted compensation."
actual_result: "19 guarded race/recovery cases pass, unchanged-base negative controls reproduce the defect, Node 26.12.1 and Bun 1.4.3 public SDK controls pass, and canonical full coverage passes 11,423 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts."
component: sdk-transactions
